{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Noah, Noah.</b> Rest for those above, rest for those below. And anyone whose name is doubled — it is certain that he is righteous, as with אברהם אברהם. And they raise an objection in the Yerushalmi: but is it not written תרח תרח? And they answer: this teaches that Terach repented." "<b>A man.</b> Rabbi Tanhuma opened: ״פרי צדיק עץ חיים״ — when Adam departed from the world without children, he is distressed and ashamed because he did not establish generations. The Holy One, blessed be He, says to him: You have the fruit of the Torah in which you toiled, as it is written of it ״פרי צדיק עץ חיים״ — it does not say 'his sons' here, but עץ חיים, and that is the Torah, which is called עץ חיים. Also this verse proves it: ״אלה תולדות נח איש צדיק״ — ״אלה תולדות נח שם וחם ויפת״ is not written here, but rather איש צדיק. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: Noah did not die until he saw the entire world settled, and he saw seventy nations issuing from his loins, and of all of them only his righteousness is mentioned, as it is said: איש צדיק תמים. It is stated in B'reshit Rabbah, chapter 30, section 6, that anyone about whom תמים is said — it is certain that his years were completed in measures of seven. And R. Yitzchak bar Avraham explained that his years go in sevenths, as we find with Abraham, of blessed memory, who lived 175 years, and Noah who lived 950 years — and these are 5 years in excess of the sevenths. One may say: it could be reckoned from the hour that תמים is said of him, namely when HaShem, may He be exalted, told him to make the ark, and he was occupied with it for 120 years. And if you wish, take note that Noah lived after the flood — here you have 950; subtract the year of the flood, which is not reckoned because the orders of creation changed in it, and the remainder goes in sevenths." "<b>He was.</b> Every place where היה is said of someone — see a new world and sustaining others. Noah, Joseph, Moses, Iyov — in all of them היה is said, and in all of them you will find these two features."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:10.456855139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}